703:   /**
704:    * Command to pin the Zeebe engine's internal clock to a specific time.
705:    *
706:    * <p>This method initiates a command to pin the clock to a specified time. You can specify the
707:    * time using either an epoch timestamp in milliseconds or an {@link java.time.Instant} object.
708:    *
709:    * <p>Once pinned, the clock will remain at the specified time and will not advance until another
710:    * <code>pin</code> or <code>reset</code> command is issued. This is useful for scenarios where
711:    * you need to simulate process execution at a specific point in time.
712:    *
713:    * <p>Example usage:
714:    *
715:    * <pre>{@code
716:    * final long pinnedTime = 1742461285000L; // Thu, Mar 20, 2025 09:01:25 GMT+0000
717:    * camundaClient
718:    *  .newClockPinCommand()
719:    *  .time(pinnedTime)
720:    *  .send();
721:    *
722:    * final Instant futureInstant = Instant.now().plus(Duration.ofDays(7));
723:    * camundaClient
724:    *  .newClockPinCommand()
725:    *  .time(futureInstant)
726:    *  .send();
727:    * }</pre>
728:    *
729:    * <p>The command is marked as <strong>experimental</strong> and may undergo changes or
730:    * improvements in future releases.
